Three.js conventions (right, up, back; quaternions in XYZW order), and a\nframe's intrinsics describe its depth grid, which can differ from the source\nimage size. Use get_asset for a fresh download link when an earlier link has\nexpired. How the tasks fit together: https://docs.atlas.worldlabs.ai/how-to-use-atlas.md\n"], "addedNames": ["Context7", "Hugging_Face", "World_Labs_Marble"], "removedNames": [], "type": "mcp_instructions_delta"}, "cwd": "/home/user/rainbow-", "entrypoint": "remote_mobile", "gitBranch": "ccr-47b10cec-03c7co", "isSidechain": true, "parentUuid": "340b9298-4511-4715-9709-d2c2eb545648", "rendered": [{"content": "<system-reminder>\n# MCP Server Instructions\n\nThe following MCP servers have provided instructions for how to use their tools and resources:\n\n## Context7\nUse this server to fetch current documentation whenever the user asks about a library, framework, SDK, API, CLI tool, or cloud service — even well-known ones like React, Next.js, Prisma, Express, Tailwind, Django, or Spring Boot. This includes API syntax, configuration, version migration, porting code between libraries, platforms, or SQL dialects, library-specific debugging, setup instructions, and CLI tool usage. Use even when you think you know the answer — your training data may not reflect recent changes. Prefer this over web search for library docs.\n\nDo not use for: refactoring, debugging, or reviewing code that does not depend on a library or platform API, or general programming concepts.\n\n## Hugging_Face\nPrefer these Hugging Face tools over web search for live Hub data; start with hf_fs.\nHugging Face tools are being used by authenticated user 'josdois'\n\n## World_Labs_Marble\nWorld Labs tools for building 3D scenes from text and images: generate images,\nestimate cameras and depth, generate new views, reconstruct Gaussian splats,\nand extract meshes. Call list_projects first: it names the projects the user\nmay work in and which of these tools each can run. Every oth